Kernel_uninstallModule
├── when the caller is not the EntryPoint Uninstall
│   └── it should revert with Unauthorized error
└── when the caller is the EntryPoint or self Uninstall
    ├── given moduleType is Validator Uninstall
    │   ├── given the validator is installed Uninstall
    │   │   └── it should clear validator hook state
    │   └── given the validator is not installed Uninstall
    │       └── it should be a no-op and leave root unchanged
    ├── given moduleType is Executor Uninstall
    │   └── it should clear executor hook
    ├── given moduleType is Fallback Uninstall
    │   └── it should clear selector config for the selector
    ├── given moduleType is Hook Uninstall
    │   └── it should disable the hook
    ├── given moduleType is Policy Uninstall
    │   ├── given the policy is the last installed policy
    │   │   └── it should pop the policy from the list
    │   └── given the policy is not the last installed policy
    │       └── it should revert with InvalidPermissionUninstallOrder error
    ├── given moduleType is Signer Uninstall
    │   ├── given policies remain installed
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidPermissionUninstallOrder error
    │   ├── given the signer does not match current signer
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidPermissionId error
    │   └── given the signer matches and no policies remain
    │       └── it should clear signer and hook state
    └── given moduleType is unsupported
        └── it should revert with NotImplemented error
